{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Apex_STEM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Apex STEM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(VERY_SLOW!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (VERY SLOW!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In how many ways can <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> juniors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seniors form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> disjoint teams of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people so \nthat each team has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> juniors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seniors? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/882e56c013aa7b4a88d21a3e9ca18496f64037f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }720\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }1350\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }2700\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }3280\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }8100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"482\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of ways in which we can choose the juniors for the team are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/971082fd3cac6762a29c78a2788dfccf46851b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${6\\choose2}{4\\choose2}{2\\choose2}=15\\cdot6\\cdot1=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"243\" height=\"55\" />. Similarly, the number of ways to choose the seniors are also 90 ways, so the total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b49e71e0a9c47344df016480fecfd5e3d1f5406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90\\cdot90=8100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />. But we must divide the number of permutations of three teams, since the order in which the teams were chosen doesn't matter, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cf13b64f701680377a1d9659ffc5791abd3b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8100}{3!}=\\frac{8100}{6}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }1350}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n~small edits by NSAoPS\n~edits by YING821\n~minor edits by Aha4525\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's first suppose that the three teams are distinguishable. The number of ways to choose the first team of two juniors and two seniors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd588fa669fe701105d60a4d03a9c8edb6f0fb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${6\\choose2}{6\\choose2} = 15\\cdot 15 = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"202\" height=\"55\" />. Now, only four juniors and four seniors are left to choose the second team. Thus, the second team can be formed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32ccaab996923d61915db55ddfedff76f55bd7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4\\choose2}{4\\choose2} = 6\\cdot 6 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"174\" height=\"55\" /> ways. There are now only two juniors and two seniors left, so the third team can only be formed in one way. Thus, the total number of ways in which we can choose two juniors and two seniors for three distinguishable teams is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c059131996649e656a49e81807431a9c0b82b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225\\cdot 36 = 8100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> ways. However, the problem does not require the teams to be distinguishable. Therefore, we must divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> to find the answer for three indistinguishable teams.\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/2217499f1d96697d4b385d995864ab75614a41f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8100}{6} =\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }1350}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~jjjxi\n</p><p>~edit by yanes04 (wrong number)\n</p><p>~ edit by RoyalPawn38\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Apex_STEM\">Video Solution by Apex STEM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Apex STEM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UOOUuVXzpgU\">https://youtu.be/UOOUuVXzpgU</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MejyLEPjC0I\">https://youtu.be/MejyLEPjC0I</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I\">https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28VERY_SLOW.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(VERY_SLOW!)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (VERY SLOW!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (VERY SLOW!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6qYaJsgqkbs?si=K2Ebwqg-Ro8Yqoiv\">https://youtu.be/6qYaJsgqkbs?si=K2Ebwqg-Ro8Yqoiv</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j-37jvqzhrg?si=IBSPzNSvdIodGvZ7&amp;t=1145\">https://youtu.be/j-37jvqzhrg?si=IBSPzNSvdIodGvZ7&amp;t=1145</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AEd5tf1PJxk\">https://youtu.be/AEd5tf1PJxk</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_o5zagJVe1U\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_o5zagJVe1U</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2EF0EDlxgkM\">https://youtu.be/2EF0EDlxgkM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video Solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=1430s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=1430s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto